## Expiry and supersession

Verdicts carry dates because they expire. "What would change this verdict"
is the trigger list above, written BEFORE the next round of data so it
cannot be fitted afterwards. When this record is superseded, mark it in
place with a dated banner pointing at the current authority - never rewrite
it, and never leave two records both reading as current: one document is
authoritative for live state and another for history, and a stale entry
that still reads as current is a defect a downstream consumer will file
(one did, in the field).
